        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Fothergilla, Clerodendrum, Fothergilla gardenii, Fothergilla major\n- Taxonomy: genera, species, flowering plants, Hamamelidaceae, Lamiaceae\n- Places: southeastern United States, Allegheny Mountains\n\nFacts:\n- Fothergilla is a genus of two or three species of flowering plants in the family Hamamelidaceae.\n- Fothergilla is native to woodlands and swamps of the southeastern United States.\n- Clerodendrum is a genus of flowering plants in the family Lamiaceae.\n- Fothergilla gardenii is one of two species in the genus Fothergilla.\n- Fothergilla major is a species of flowering plant in the genus Fothergilla and the family Hamamelidaceae.\n- Fothergilla major is native to woodlands and swamps in the Allegheny Mountains of the southeastern United States.",
